> What are you considering the "important things"?  For the purposes of
> getting out of Gehennom, I'd put here only BoH, luckstone, and any rings or
> boots that need to be swapped.

I would consider the unicorn horn the single most important item to 
remain blessed.  One *can* allow it to become uncursed (not in slashem) 
but then has to be very careful about any additional cursing, a risk I 
prefer to avoid. (If it gets cursed and you apply it to heal blindness, 
you might become ill.)  My BoH usually stays in a sack most of the time 
I am carrying the amulet, so it will not get uncursed or cursed.  If it 
gets uncursed during the short time outside, I will of course rebless it 
immediately, in order to avoid getting burdened (or worse, if it happens 
to catch a second curse later).  Rings, yes.  Boots, I don't usually 
swap them anymore on the ascension run (don't like levitation boots, 
will wish for a ring of levitation if necessary).  And of course, if 
your weapon is two-handed, you'll have to keep it blessed all the time.

I would not care to bless the luckstone if it gets uncursed.  If it gets 
cursed, I would put it in a bag until I use one of my scrolls of remove 
curse to uncurse a bunch of stuff. Most items that I carry will be 
blessed when the ascension run begins, most will work well uncursed, too 
(stethoscope, magic whistle), so I will let them get cursed first before 
intervening.

So the two things to be kept blessed (outside your bag, that is) are, 
IMO, the unicorn horn and a two-handed wielded weapon.  Everything else 
may get uncursed, and some stuff may even get cursed without any problem.

By the way, if food rations get cursed, will they be more likely to 
render you unconscious or count as "rotten food"?  And conversely, will 
blessed food never make you unconscious?
